The Chinese customs regulations stipulate that each batch of a certain type of product must undergo five consecutive inspections before export. If two indicators are found to be non-compliant, the batch cannot be exported, and the remaining inspections will not be conducted. It is known that the probability of failing any given inspection is 0.2. A batch of products is now being inspected for export.  
